<%#
  Offered wherever the visit already holds more than one sheet: the sheet that
  was just generated, and the entry panel the visit returns to for the next one.

  `surface` is required and names which of the two rendered it — `sheet` on the
  page that crossed two, `entry` on the panel it came back to. Both places
  report the one event, so the attribute is the only thing that says whether the
  sheet or the panel is the placement a visit answers; a caller that omits it
  raises rather than reporting an unlabelled showing.

  The server decides, from the visit it holds in the session, so every tab of the
  visit sees the same set and the offer is part of the markup a restored page
  replays. Accepting gathers the visit's sheets in generation order; the same
  route takes one sheet or a set of them.

  The offer is an outcome the server renders into a page rather than into a
  frame, so it reports on the load that follows this response, and the response
  names itself in `data-analytics-response-key` so a snapshot Turbo replays
  cannot report the same offer twice.
%>
<% if visit.offer_pending? %>
  <div class="songbook-prompt no-print <%= local_assigns[:class_name] %>"
       data-analytics-page-response="Songbook Offer Shown"
       data-analytics-offer-surface="<%= surface %>"
       data-analytics-response-key="<%= visit.offer_key %>">
    <p class="songbook-prompt-message" role="status">
      <%= t("shared.songbook_prompt.message", count: visit.sheet_count) %>
    </p>

    <%= button_to t("shared.songbook_prompt.action"),
          songbooks_path,
          params: { lyric_tokens: visit.sheets },
          class: "button button-primary button-songbook",
          form: { data: { turbo_frame: "_top" } } %>

    <%# The answer settles the offer for the rest of the visit, and the visit is
        the server's, so the next page it renders leaves the offer out. %>
    <%= button_to t("shared.songbook_prompt.dismiss"),
          songbook_offer_path,
          method: :delete,
          class: "songbook-prompt-dismiss",
          form: { data: { turbo_frame: "_top", analytics_umami_submit: "Songbook Offer Dismissed" } } %>
  </div>
<% end %>
